On completion of this course, students will be able to:
1. Have a good knowledge of shopping mall business in terms of management and investment;
2. Understand the revenue model of the shopping mall business, its customer service and brand management;
3. Know the regulatory framework of the shopping mall business;
4. Participate in the construction and management of a hypothetical shopping mall.
Measurement of Learning Outcomes
1. Development of a hypothetical shopping mall. Students in groups are expected to write a leasing proposal and budget.
2. Class assignments are used to test students' understanding of specific concepts and practices.
3. Final examination specifically requires students to apply knowledge and past learning in addressing the case and examination questions

Upon completion of this course, students should be able to:
o Understand the land tenure system in Hong Kong and apply the knowledge of land use control in real estate settings in a global context;
o Know the two dimensional development control: lease control and statutory control in Hong Kong, the role of various authorities in the land development control;
o Understand and apply town planning, land control and development knowledge to delivering excellent services to potential clients;
o Develop creative thinking and problem solving skills relevant to land development issues;
o self-managed ability, leadership skills, team work spirit, analytical and communicative skills and oral presentation skills that are appropriate in a variety of investment scenarios through case studies and group projects;
o Identify and address ethical issues in both land investment and development settings.

Upon completion of this course, students should be able to:
• Understand the fundamental principles of property returns, the key concepts and the important relations underlying commercial real estate and property cashflows
• Understand the nature of return and risk quantification and characteristics of property investment appraisals;
• Understand financial modelling techniques and how to apply them to evaluate investment returns;
• Develop robust, fully integrated financial forecasting models, which include sensitivity analysis and data tables
• Critically analyze and evaluate investment appraisals;
• Understand and apply the knowledge of property investment analysis skills to real world practices and deliver excellent services to potential clients, making informed investment decisions;
• Develop creative thinking, self-managed ability, team work spirit, analytical and communicative skills through case studies and project presentations.

